{
  "title": "Modified type Product to carry a stock count",
  "diff": [
    "diff --git a/src/types/product.ts b/src/types/product.ts",
    "--- a/src/types/product.ts",
    "+++ b/src/types/product.ts",
    "@@ -5,0 +6 @@ export interface Product {",
    "+  stock: number"
  ],
  "codegraph": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "title": "Stock count on the product type",
        "context": [
          "A product now has a stock count: the number of units the shop has of it. The change is to the shape of a product only. No page shows the count, and nothing reads it before a product goes into the cart. The catalogue request does not check that the server sends the count.",
          "",
          "## Overview",
          "",
          "- **When** a shopper opens the catalogue, **then** nothing changes.",
          "- **When** a shopper adds a product to the cart, **then** nothing changes.",
          "- **When** the server sends a product with no stock count, **then** nothing changes.",
          "- **When** code builds a product with no stock count, **then** [the type checker reports that `stock` is not there](code:src/types/product.ts#Product).",
          "",
          "## Implementation",
          "",
          "**`src/types/product.ts`**",
          "",
          "- Modified [`Product`](code:src/types/product.ts#Product) to require a property `stock: number`."
        ],
        "kind": "entry",
